2026-09-27T03:27:30.2119149Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2119644Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2120082Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2121303Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2122664Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2122786Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2123080Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2123486Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2124132Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2124286Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2124603Z ================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2124794Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2125021Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2125588Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2125918Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2126096Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2126509Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2126763Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2126980Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2127543Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2128054Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2213212Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2214496Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2214696Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2215421Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2216263Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2216679Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2217109Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2217695Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2217820Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2218279Z ========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2218429Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2220341Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2222333Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2222644Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2223321Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2224187Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2225031Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2225855Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2226485Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2226873Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2227444Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2227810Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2228028Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2229591Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2231619Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2232578Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2234091Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:27:30.2234423Z 
